name  Secrets
theme facility
spawn 3.5 3.5 0
entity i imp
entity c crystal
# A6, one thing at a time. Walk up to each and press F.
#
#   The door at 7,4 divides the map and wants key.red. Nobody here carries one,
#   so it refuses and names the key it wants — that is the whole locked-door
#   contract: the world stores WHICH key, and the game layer decides whether
#   you hold it (meatray/game/secrets.lua). The imp east of it is out of reach
#   until something gives you the key.
#
#   The vault's north wall at 4,9 slides two tiles north when pushed, opening
#   the way in. A push-wall is a solid tile that walks: it emits a shape change
#   for the cell it leaves and the one it takes, so collision, rays, gas and
#   light all stay right without any of them knowing it exists.
#
#   Standing inside the vault counts the secret. The ROOM is the secret, not
#   the wall — blow your way in with a grenade instead and it scores the same.
lock 7 4 key.red
pushwall 4 9 0 -1 2
secret 3 9 4 10 vault
---
